 viability assay. Data are presented as the mean ± SEM of three independent experiments and analyzed by one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey’s post hoc test. Statistical significance: ** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01 and *** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001 vs. control for 24 h; ### <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001 vs. control for 48 h. A two-way ANOVA followed by a Bonferroni post hoc test analyzed the time-dependent effects of ROT. Statistical significance: $ <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, $$ <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01, and $$$ <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001. (<bold>b</bold>) Cells were incubated in the absence or presence of ROT (0.5 μM) for 48 h and then treated with hADSC-CM or NI-hADSC-CM at 100 or 50 or 25% during the last 24 h, and cell survival was assessed by trypan blue assay. Data are presented as the mean ± SEM of three independent experiments. Statistical analysis was performed using one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey’s post hoc test. Statistical significance: a—compared with control; b—compared with ROT; * <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, ** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01, and *** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="ijms-22-02322-g001.jpg"><?image-name ijms-22-02322-g001.jpg?><?image-size 88138?><?image-md5 8a8d75ef48611fe568a667a7fd40c256?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 2168?><?image-original-width 2096?><?image-scaled-height 722?><?image-scaled-width 698?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/8a8d75ef4861/ijms-22-02322-g001.jpg?><?thumb-name ijms-22-02322-g001.gif?><?thumb-size 5036?><?thumb-md5 5e28eced2b1631e64cff1523b2148a2b?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 103?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/5e28eced2b16/ijms-22-02322-g001.gif?></graphic></fig><fig id="ijms-22-02322-f002" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Effects of NI-hADSC-CM against ROT on TH and Syn211 protein expressions. SH-SY5Y cells were seeded at a density of 5 × 10<sup>4</sup> cells/mL in DMEM containing 1% FBS and used for the experiments after overnight incubation. Cells incubated in the absence or presence of ROT (0.5 μM) for 48 h were treated with hADSC-CM (50%) or NI-hADSC-CM (50%) during the last 24 h, and the TH (<bold>a</bold>), Syn211 (<bold>b</bold>), and GAPDH or β-actin expression levels were assessed by Western blotting. Images are representative of three independent experiments. Data are presented as the mean ± SEM of three independent experiments. Statistical analysis was performed using one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey’s post hoc test. Statistical significance: a—compared with control; b—compared with ROT; * <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, ** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01, and *** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="ijms-22-02322-g002.jpg"><?image-name ijms-22-02322-g002.jpg?><?image-size 44884?><?image-md5 bbd42defbfd500469a6e0dc0d8c9f26c?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 1276?><?image-original-width 3320?><?image-scaled-height 283?><?image-scaled-width 737?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/bbd42defbfd5/ijms-22-02322-g002.jpg?><?thumb-name ijms-22-02322-g002.gif?><?thumb-size 7695?><?thumb-md5 b072b70dad7e0e01e9378066d070fe80?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 77?><?thumb-scaled-width 200?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/b072b70dad7e/ijms-22-02322-g002.gif?></graphic></fig><fig id="ijms-22-02322-f003" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Effects of NI-hADSC-CM against ROT on p-S129 and total α-syn expressions in Triton X-100-soluble cell lysate fractions. SH-SY5Y cells were seeded at a density of 5 × 10<sup>4</sup> cells/mL in DMEM containing 1% FBS and used for the experiments after overnight incubation. Cells incubated in the absence or presence of ROT (0.5 μM) for 48 h were treated with NI-hADSC-CM (50%) during the last 24 h. Cell lysates were prepared as 1% Triton X-100 soluble and insoluble (2× SDS-soluble) fractions. The expression levels of p-S129- and total α-syn were analyzed from 1% Triton X-100 soluble fractions by Western blotting using 12 and 8% SDS-PAGE gels (<bold>a</bold>). Images are representative of three independent experiments. The bar graphs represent fold changes in p-S129 α-syn/GAPDH (<bold>b</bold>,<bold>d</bold>) and total α-syn/GAPDH (<bold>c</bold>,<bold>e</bold>) in 12% (<bold>b</bold>,<bold>c</bold>) or 8% (<bold>d</bold>,<bold>e</bold>) SDS-PAGE. Data are presented as the mean ± SEM of three independent experiments. Statistical analysis was performed using one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey’s post hoc test. Statistical significance: a—compared with control; b—compared with ROT; * <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01, ** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, and *** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="ijms-22-02322-g003.jpg"><?image-name ijms-22-02322-g003.jpg?><?image-size 146072?><?image-md5 5425d93d3a74af53e2783fe75e2c8b7d?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 4352?><?image-original-width 2944?><?image-scaled-height 1088?><?image-scaled-width 736?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/5425d93d3a74/ijms-22-02322-g003.jpg?><?thumb-name ijms-22-02322-g003.gif?><?thumb-size 4729?><?thumb-md5 aaad99cb693b9046ce4e27bd15b4e983?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 148?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/aaad99cb693b/ijms-22-02322-g003.gif?></graphic></fig><fig id="ijms-22-02322-f004" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Effects of NI-hADSC-CM against ROT on p-S129 and total α-syn expressions in Triton X-100-insoluble cell lysate fractions. SH-SY5Y cells were seeded at a density of 5 × 10<sup>4</sup> cells/mL in DMEM containing 1% FBS and used for experiments after overnight incubation. Cells incubated in the absence or presence of ROT (0.5 μM) for 48 h were treated with NI-hADSC-CM (50%) during the last 24 h. Cell lysates were prepared as 1% Triton X-100 soluble and insoluble (2× SDS-soluble) fractions. The expression levels of p-S129- and total α-syn were analyzed from 1% Triton X-100 insoluble (2× SDS soluble) fractions by Western blotting using 12 and 8% SDS-PAGE gels (<bold>a</bold>). Images are representative of three independent experiments. The bar graphs represent fold changes in p-S129 α-syn/GAPDH (<bold>b</bold>,<bold>d</bold>) and total α-syn/GAPDH (<bold>c</bold>,<bold>e</bold>) in 12% (<bold>b</bold>,<bold>c</bold>) or 8% (<bold>e</bold>) SDS-PAGE gels. Data are presented as the mean ± SEM of three independent experiments. Statistical analysis was performed using one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey’s post hoc test. Statistical significance: a—compared with control; b—compared with ROT; * <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, ** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01, and *** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="ijms-22-02322-g004.jpg"><?image-name ijms-22-02322-g004.jpg?><?image-size 137545?><?image-md5 2040cd5b5ceb78802f31ca569a4128b8?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 4924?><?image-original-width 2964?><?image-scaled-height 1231?><?image-scaled-width 741?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/2040cd5b5ceb/ijms-22-02322-g004.jpg?><?thumb-name ijms-22-02322-g004.gif?><?thumb-size 10010?><?thumb-md5 41ce828f56ff1db47ae7542152d7e8b3?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 166?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/41ce828f56ff/ijms-22-02322-g004.gif?></graphic></fig><fig id="ijms-22-02322-f005" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Effects of NI-hADSC-CM against ROT on protein expression of neuronal markers. SH-SY5Y cells were seeded at a density of 5 × 10<sup>4</sup> cells/mL in DMEM containing 1% FBS and used for experiments after overnight incubation. Cells in the absence or presence of ROT (0.5 μM) for 48 h were treated with hADSC-CM (50%) or NI-hADSC-CM (50%) during the last 24 h, and the expression levels of NF-H (<bold>a</bold>), β3-tubulin (<bold>b</bold>), NeuN (<bold>c</bold>), SYP (<bold>d</bold>), and GAPDH or β-actin were analyzed by Western blotting. Images are representative of three independent experiments. Data are presented as mean ± SEM of three independent experiments. Statistical analysis was performed using one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey’s post hoc test. Statistical significance: a—compared with control; b—compared with ROT; * <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, ** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01, and *** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="ijms-22-02322-g005.jpg"><?image-name ijms-22-02322-g005.jpg?><?image-size 95992?><?image-md5 ea5bf8405f1254a90276741719593529?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 2380?><?image-original-width 3104?><?image-scaled-height 595?><?image-scaled-width 776?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/ea5bf8405f12/ijms-22-02322-g005.jpg?><?thumb-name ijms-22-02322-g005.gif?><?thumb-size 5458?><?thumb-md5 e2a29ea54baf41dd44bea0c3f2c1841d?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 80?><?thumb-scaled-width 104?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/e2a29ea54baf/ijms-22-02322-g005.gif?></graphic></fig><fig id="ijms-22-02322-f006" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Effects of NI-hADSC-CM against ROT on Bcl-2 family proteins and Cyt-c expressions. SH-SY5Y cells were seeded at a density of 5 × 10<sup>4</sup> cells/mL in DMEM containing 1% FBS and used for experiments after overnight incubation. Cells in the absence or presence of ROT (0.5 μM) for 48 h were treated with hADSC-CM (50%) or NI-hADSC-CM (50%) during the last 24 h and the Bax (<bold>a</bold>), Bcl-2 (<bold>b</bold>), Mcl-1 (<bold>c</bold>), Cyt-c (<bold>d</bold>) and β-actin or GAPDH expression levels were assessed by Western blotting. Images are representative of three independent experiments. Data are presented as mean ± SEM of three independent experiments. Statistical analysis was performed using one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey’s post hoc test. Statistical significance: a—compared with control; b—compared with ROT; * <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, ** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01, and *** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="ijms-22-02322-g006.jpg"><?image-name ijms-22-02322-g006.jpg?><?image-size 93878?><?image-md5 98b0ea4114ff412443f01031c3b3449d?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 2440?><?image-original-width 3084?><?image-scaled-height 610?><?image-scaled-width 771?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/98b0ea4114ff/ijms-22-02322-g006.jpg?><?thumb-name ijms-22-02322-g006.gif?><?thumb-size 5196?><?thumb-md5 6341f5fc5bd53a09431e7e5e17f10c46?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 80?><?thumb-scaled-width 101?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/6341f5fc5bd5/ijms-22-02322-g006.gif?></graphic></fig><fig id="ijms-22-02322-f007" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Effects of NI-hADSC-CM against ROT on caspases and PARP-1 protein expressions. SH-SY5Y cells were seeded at a density of 5 × 10<sup>4</sup> cells/mL in DMEM containing 1% FBS and used for experiments after overnight incubation. Cells in the absence or presence of ROT (0.5 μM) for 48 h were treated with hADSC-CM (50%) or NI-hADSC-CM (50%) during the last 24 h, and the expression levels of pro-Cas-9 (<bold>a</bold>), pro-Cas-3 (<bold>b</bold>), pro-Cas-7 (<bold>c</bold>), PARP (<bold>d</bold>), and β-actin or GAPDH were assessed by Western blotting. Images are representative of three independent experiments. Data are presented as the mean ± SEM of three independent experiments. Statistical analysis was performed using one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey’s post hoc test. Statistical significance: a—compared with control; b—compared with ROT; * <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, ** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.01, and *** <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.001.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="ijms-22-02322-g007.jpg"><?image-name ijms-22-02322-g007.jpg?><?image-size 93449?><?image-md5 2b72f76582d0201220945866276e7f59?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 2328?><?image-original-width 3064?><?image-scaled-height 582?><?image-scaled-width 766?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/2b72f76582d0/ijms-22-02322-g007.jpg?><?thumb-name ijms-22-02322-g007.gif?><?thumb-size 5250?><?thumb-md5 ddd975b8c2be6f6ebb8929838e10a7e8?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 80?><?thumb-scaled-width 105?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/ddd975b8c2be/ijms-22-02322-g007.gif?></graphic></fig><fig id="ijms-22-02322-f008" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Figure 8</label><caption><p>Diagrammatic representation of various activities of NI-hADSC-CM in the ROT-induced PD-like model. The downward arrows (↓) denote inhibitions, and the upward arrows (↑) denote stimulation by ROT (red) and NI-hADSC-CM (green).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="ijms-22-02322-g008.jpg"><?image-name ijms-22-02322-g008.jpg?><?image-size 126419?><?image-md5 c332bb9544edafcd285e7fa6fae086d6?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 2156?><?image-original-width 3068?><?image-scaled-height 539?><?image-scaled-width 767?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/c332bb9544ed/ijms-22-02322-g008.jpg?><?thumb-name ijms-22-02322-g008.gif?><?thumb-size 4720?><?thumb-md5 4f7f7b562927f5d47bc922e9fb61d0e2?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 79?><?thumb-scaled-width 113?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/df49/7956615/4f7f7b562927/ijms-22-02322-g008.gif?></graphic></fig></floats-group></article>